Steps for Jenkins job:
a.	Create the global username & password credentials for dockerhub credentials and store as: username and password
b.	Create the environment variables in the job:
i.	Environment var section
ii.	Select option: Use secret text(s) or file(s) 
iii.	Select Bindings: 
Username and password (separated) 
iv.	Provide the env var name as: 
a)	DOCKER_USER 
b)	DOCKER_PASS
c.	Add the below commands to login and push the image in execute shell commands:
i.	docker build -t saodocker1/bbwebapp:01 .
ii.	#docker stop app
iii.	#docker rm app
iv.	#docker run -d --name app -p 9090:8080 saodocker1/bbwebapp:01
v.	#echo "container started"
vi.	echo "$DOCKER_PASS" | docker login -u "$DOCKER_USER" --password-stdin
vii.	docker push saodocker1/bbwebapp:01
viii.	echo "image pushed successfully"
d.	Save and build the job. Observe the image pushed on docker hub registry

