LAB 11: Integrate Kubernetes (AKS) with Jenkins for Deployment
Objective: Configure Jenkins to interact with Azure AKS and deploy Kubernetes manifests directly from Jenkins.
a.	Install Kubernetes CLI on Jenkins VM
curl -LO https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl
chmod +x kubectl
sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/
kubectl version --client
b.	On Jenkins VM: 
i.	Install Azure CLI:
curl -sL https://aka.ms/InstallAzureCLIDeb | sudo bash
az version
ii.	Login to Azure: 
az login 
iii.	Configure AKS Access on Jenkins Server
az aks get-credentials \
--resource-group <rg-name> \
--name <aks-name>
iv.	Verify access:
kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A    
v.	Here, This creates ~/.kube/config which Jenkins will use.
Grant Jenkins Permission to Use kubeconfig
sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/jenkins/.kube
sudo cp ~/.kube/config /var/lib/jenkins/.kube/config
sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /var/lib/jenkins/.kube
vi. Restart Jenkins:
sudo systemctl restart jenkins     
